;
; RTL81598.INF - usb-wdm-free RTL815X: Realtek RTL8152/RTL8153 USB
; Ethernet in vendor mode, Windows 98 SE and ME (ethernet.md sections 4.4,
; 7.1, 7.4). NDIS.VXD loads the WDM miniport (DevLoader=*ndis,
; DeviceVxDs). A $Chicago$ INF is refused for Net on Windows 2000
; (cdcnet's 2000 run), so RTL815X.INF is the 2000 INF. Written from the
; Windows 2000 DDK network guide's INF pages and the Windows 98 DDK
; documentation; no DDK sample INF was read.
;
; Whole-device hardware ids: each is a dedicated network device whose
; configuration with a vendor-class first interface RTL815X selects
; (ethernet.md 5.1, 6.5). The ids are those of Linux r8152.c at f47d2236
; except 0BDA:8155, 8156, 8157 and 815A, the 2.5/5/10 Gb/s parts (RTL8156
; and later, not served yet). Another id in this list carrying such a chip
; is refused at start (unknown chip version), with an event-log entry.
; 0BDA:8153 moves here from CDCNET.INF's 98 SE/ME/2000 models when this
; package ships (owner decision, ethernet.md 6.5).

[Version]
Signature="$Chicago$"
Class=Net
ClassGUID={4D36E972-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%Provider%
DriverVer=10/24/2026,0.1.0.0

[Manufacturer]
%Provider%=Models

